{"body":"## Problem

The code-review path gathers PR metadata, refs, changed files, diff statistics, checks, and review threads through many small tool calls. The commands are usually fast, but each call extends the LLM → tool → LLM loop.

In a seven-day production sample of 394 reviewer sessions:

- 7,474 Bash calls had a 40 ms median and 1.29 s p95;
- Bash execution represented only about 3.3% of total wall-clock;
- duration correlated strongly with span count (0.87) and output tokens (0.981);
- sessions at or below 3 minutes had a median of 22 spans, while 5–8 minute sessions had 65.

## Proposed change

Add one deterministic startup operation that builds a compact, typed review-context bundle containing:

- repository and PR identity;
- base SHA, head SHA, and last-reviewed SHA when present;
- changed files and bounded diff statistics/content references;
- relevant check state;
- existing verdict and unresolved review threads;
- first-review versus re-review/delta metadata.

The reviewer should consume this bundle before analysis instead of rediscovering the same information through many small Bash/GitHub calls. Large payloads must be summarized or referenced safely rather than exported wholesale into model context.

## Acceptance criteria

- Normal review startup uses one observable context-builder operation.
- The output has a versioned, typed contract with explicit bounds and truncation metadata.
- Re-reviews receive an explicit delta from the last-reviewed SHA where available.
- GitHub pagination, unavailable refs, large diffs, deleted branches, and partial API failures are handled deterministically.
- Review prompts consume the bundle and avoid redundant discovery unless a concrete missing field requires a targeted follow-up.
- Telemetry records builder duration, source request counts, payload size, truncation, cache use, and targeted follow-up count.
- Tests cover small, large, generated-file-heavy, first-review, and re-review pull requests.
- Production verification reports median/p75/p90, spans per session, ≤3-minute attainment, and review-quality guardrails.

## Target

Bring the normal and re-review path to a wall-clock median of 3 minutes or less without weakening review coverage.

_Reported from FortuneOS production measurements on behalf of Art._","number":605,"state":"OPEN","title":"Build a deterministic startup context bundle for code review","url":"https://github.com/awinogradov/code-assistants/issues/605"}

